inventory: The hosts and groups, with their values, and host patterns.

An inventory is a file in inventories/, such as
inventories/production.yaml, or a key in inventories of winch.yaml. It
holds data and secrets, but no templates or expressions.

```yaml
# inventories/production.yaml
hosts:
  mail.acme.com:
    address: 192.0.2.10
  monitor.acme.com:
    address: 192.0.2.20
groups:
  all:
    user: admin
    vars:
      domain: acme.com
  mail:
    hosts: [mail.acme.com]
    vars:
      mail_server: true
```

```yaml
# winch.yaml
name: acme
vars:
  domain: example.com
  mail_server: false
steps:
  - name: Install postfix on the mail servers
    pkg:
      name: postfix
    when: !expr vars.mail_server
```

--inventory <name> names the inventory of a run, and inventory in
winch.yaml names a default. A project with one inventory uses it. A
project with more inventories and no default makes each run name its
inventory, so a run against production is always deliberate.

The group all contains every host. A host value beats a group value,
and a group value beats a value of all. Two groups of one host that set
different values for one variable, or for user, are an error, unless
the host sets that value too.

Every other SSH setting, such as the port or the key, comes from the
SSH config of the controller. Its Host blocks match the host name, also
when the host has an address.

Host patterns select hosts, in the hosts of a stage, in --hosts, and in
winch run and winch exec:

    web          the hosts in the group web, or the host named web
    web,db       the hosts in web or in db
    web & prod   the hosts in web and in prod
    web & !web3  the hosts in web, without web3

& and ! bind tighter than ",". Hosts keep inventory order. A name that
is neither a group nor a host is an error. A pattern with only ! names
is an error: write all & !web, not !web.

Keys:
  hosts          map              -  The hosts, by name.
  hosts.address  string           -  The host name or IP for SSH.
  hosts.user     string           -  The SSH login user.
  hosts.vars     map              -  Variable values for the host.
  groups         map              -  The groups, by name.
  groups.user    string           -  The SSH login user of the hosts of the group.
  groups.hosts   list of strings  -  The member hosts.
  groups.vars    map              -  Variable values for the hosts of the group.

Run "winch doc inventory.<key>" for the full text of a key.
